messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nNo students who work in the library are from the computer science department. All students who have part-time jobs offered by the university are students who work in the library. All students who take the database course are from the computer science department. All students instructed by professor David are taking the database course. All students working in the lab are instructed by professor David. James is a student working in the lab. Jack neither has a part-time job offered by the university nor works in the lab.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? James has a part-time job offered by the university.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>\nTo determine if the statement "James has a part-time job offered by the university" is true, false, or uncertain, we need to analyze the given information step by step:\n\n1.**No students who work in the library are from the computer science department.**\n   - This means if a student works in the library, they cannot be from the computer science department.\n\n2.**All students who have part-time jobs offered by the university are students who work in the library.**\n   - This implies that if a student has a part-time job offered by the university, they must work in the library.\n\n3.**All students who take the database course are from the computer science department.**\n   - This means if a student takes the database course, they must be from the computer science department.\n\n4.**All students instructed by professor David are taking the database course.**\n   - This means if a student is instructed by professor David, they are taking the database course.\n\n5.**All students working in the lab are instructed by professor David.**\n   - This means if a student works in the lab, they are instructed by professor David.\n\n6.**James is a student working in the lab.**\n   - From point 5, we know that James is instructed by professor David.\n\n7.**All students instructed by professor David are taking the database course.**\n   - Since James is instructed by professor David, he must be taking the database course.\n\n8.**All students who take the database course are from the computer science department.**\n   - Since James is taking the database course, he must be from the computer science department.\n\n9.**No students who work in the library are from the computer science department.**\n   - Since James is from the computer science department, he cannot work in the library.\n\n10.**James is a student working in the lab.**\n    - Since James is working in the lab, he cannot work in the library (from point 9).\n\n11.**All students working in the lab are instructed by professor David.**\n    - Since James is working in the lab, he is instructed by professor David.\n\n12.**All students instructed by professor David are taking the database course.**\n    - Since James is instructed by professor David, he is taking the database course.\n\n13.**All students who take the database course are from the computer science department.**\n    - Since James is taking the database course, he is from the computer science department.\n\n14.**James is from the computer science department.**\n    - James is from the computer science department.\n\n15.**No students who work in the library are from the computer science department.**\n    - Since James is from the computer science department, he cannot work in the library.\n\n16.**James is working in the lab.**\n    - James is working in the lab.\n\n17.**All students working in the lab are instructed by professor David.**\n    - James is instructed by professor David.\n\n18.**All students instructed by professor David are taking the database course.**\n    - James is taking the database course.\n\n19.**All