- From the statement "If an animal has legs, then it jumps," we know that if KiKi has legs, then KiKi jumps.\n   - From the statement "If an animal is terricolous, then it has legs," we know that if KiKi is terricolous, then KiKi has legs.\nIf KiKi has legs, then KiKi jumps. If KiKi is terricolous, then KiKi has legs. Therefore, if KiKi has legs, then KiKi is terricolous.\n\nEvaluate the conditional statement:\nIf KiKi jumps and has legs, then KiKi is not terricolous. If KiKi does not have legs, then KiKi is not terricolous. If KiKi has legs, then KiKi is not terricolous.\n\nConclusion:\nSince the conditional statement "If KiKi jumps and has legs, then KiKi is not terricolous" is true, and we know that if KiKi does not have legs, then KiKi is not terricolous, we can conclude that KiKi does not have legs. If KiKi does not have legs, then KiKi is not terricolous.\n\nTherefore, based on the given information, the statement "KiKi is terricolous" is false.\n\n<｜Assistant｜> <answer>\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
