messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIf something is a deadly disease, then its survival rate is low. All severe cancers are deadly diseases. Bile duct cancer is a severe cancer. All Cholangiocarcinoma is bile duct cancer. No one with mild flu has a low survival rate. If colorectal cancer is a bile duct cancer and the survival rate is low, then colorectal cancer is not a bile duct cancer.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Colorectal cancer is a severe cancer\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>.\nTo determine if the statement "Colorectal cancer is a severe cancer" is true, false, or uncertain based on the given context, let\'s break down the information step by step:.\n\n1.**Deadly Disease and Survival Rate**: .\n   - If something is a deadly disease, then its survival rate is low.\n   - All severe cancers are deadly diseases.\n   - Bile duct cancer is a severe cancer.\n   - All Cholangiocarcinoma is bile duct cancer.\n   - No one with mild flu has a low survival rate.\n   - If colorectal cancer is a bile duct cancer and the survival rate is low, then colorectal cancer is not a bile duct cancer.\n\n2.**Analyzing the Given Information**:.\n   - We know that Bile duct cancer is a severe cancer.\n   - Cholangiocarcinoma is a type of bile duct cancer.\n   - Colorectal cancer is a type of bile duct cancer (from the given statement).\n\n3.**Survival Rate and Colorectal Cancer**:.\n   - If colorectal cancer is a bile duct cancer and the survival rate is low, then colorectal cancer is not a bile duct cancer.\n   - This implies that if colorectal cancer is a bile duct cancer, its survival rate cannot be low.Colorectal cancer is not considered a severe cancer in any way.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
