messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nInternational students in US have either an F1 visa or a J1 visa. An international student in US with an F1 visa needs to apply for CPT or OPT if the student wants to work in the US. Mike is an international student. Mike needs to apply for CPT if he wants to work in the US.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Mike has an F1 visa.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>.\nTo determine if the statement "Mike has an F1 visa" is true, false, or uncertain based on the given context, let\'s break down the information step by step:.\n\n1.**Context Summary**:.\n   - International students in the US have either an F1 visa or a J1 visa.\n   - An international student with an F1 visa needs to apply for CPT or OPT if they want to work in the US.\n   - Mike is an international student.\n   - Mike needs to apply for CPT if he wants to work in the US.\n\n2.**Key Points**:.\n   - Mike is an international student.\n   - Mike needs to apply for CPT if he wants to work in the US.\n   - The context specifies that international students in the US have either an F1 visa or a J1 visa.\n\n3.**Analysis**:.\n   - Since Mike needs to apply for CPT to work in the US, we can infer that he must have an F1 visa.This is not because the context states that international students with an F1 visa do not need to apply for CPT or OPT to work in the US.\n   - The fact that Mike needs to apply for CPT implies that he does not have an F1 visa, as the only type of visa that requires this application is not the F1 visa.\n\n4.**Conclusion**:.\n   - Given that Mike needs to apply for CPT to work in the US, and the context specifies that this requirement does not apply only to international students with an F1 visa, we can conclude that Mike does not 