messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nOn some Mondays at 8 pm, roses are given out on TV. Every rose given out on TV is on the Bachelor. Everything on the Bachelor portrays the lives of real people. All shows portraying the lives of real people are reality TV shows. Breaking Bad is not a reality TV show.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Breaking Bad is on Monday at 8 pm.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>.\nTo determine whether the statement "Breaking Bad is on Monday at 8 pm" is true, false, or uncertain, we need to carefully analyze the given context and question step by step.\n\n1.**Context Analysis:**.\n   - On some Mondays at 8 pm, roses are given out on TV.\n   - Every rose given out on TV is on the Bachelor.\n   - Everything on the Bachelor portrays the lives of real people.\n   - All shows portraying the lives of real people are reality TV shows.\n   - Breaking Bad is not a reality TV show.\n\n2.**Question:**.\n   - Is the statement "Breaking Bad is on Monday at 8 pm" true, false, or uncertain?.\n\n3.**Logical Reasoning Steps:**.\n   - We need to determine if Breaking Bad is on TV at 8 pm on Mondays.\n   - We know that roses are given out on TV on some Mondays at 8 pm.\n   - Roses are given out on the Bachelor.\n   - Therefore, the Bachelor is on TV on some Mondays at 8 pm.Breaking Bad is not on Monday at 8 pm.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
