messages:   64%|######4   | 131/204 [02:40<01:16,  1.04s/it][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\n"Stranger Things" is a popular Netflix show. If a Netflix show is popular, Karen will binge-watch it. If and only if Karen binge-watches a Netflix show, she will download it. Karen does not download "Black Mirror". "Black Mirror" is a Netflix show. If Karen binge-watches a Netflix show, she will share it to Lisa.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? "Black Mirror" is popular.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>.\nTo determine if the statement "Black Mirror is popular" is true, false, or uncertain, we need to carefully analyze the given context and question step by step.Let\'s break down the information provided:.\n\n1.**"Stranger Things" is a popular Netflix show.**.\n   - This is given directly in the context.\n\n2.**If a Netflix show is popular, Karen will binge-watch it.**.\n   - This means that if a show is popular, Karen will watch it.\n\n3.**If and only if Karen binge-watches a Netflix show, she will download it.**.\n   - This is a biconditional statement, meaning:.\n     - Karen downloads a show if and only if she binge-watches it.\n     - If Karen does not download a show, she did not binge-watch it.\n\n4.**Karen does not download "Black Mirror".**.\n   - From the biconditional statement, if Karen does not download "Black Mirror", she did not binge-watch it.\n\n5.**"Black Mirror" is a Netflix show.**.\n   - This is explicitly stated in the context.If Karen does not binge-watch a Netflix show, she will not share it with Lisa.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
