messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nAll mammals are animals. All monkeys are mammals. An animal is either a monkey or a bird. All birds fly. All animals breathe. If something can fly, then it has wings. If Rock is neither a fly nor a bird, then Rock neither flies nor breathes.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Rock does not have wings.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>.\nTo determine if the statement "Rock does not have wings" is true, false, or uncertain based on the given context, let\'s break down the information step by step:.\n\n1.**All mammals are animals.**.\n   - This establishes a direct relationship between mammals and animals.\n\n2.**All monkeys are mammals.**.\n   - This means that monkeys are a subset of mammals.\n\n3.**An animal is either a monkey or a bird.**.\n   - This implies that animals can be categorized into two groups: monkeys and birds.\n\n4.**All birds fly.**.\n   - This establishes that birds have the ability to fly.\n\n5.**All animals breathe.**.\n   - This establishes that animals have the ability to breathe.\n\n6.**If something can fly, then it has wings.**.\n   - This is a conditional statement that links the ability to fly with the presence of wings.\n\n7.**If Rock is neither a fly nor a bird, then Rock neither flies nor breathes.**.\n   - This conditional statement provides a condition for Rock based on its classification.\n\nNow, let\'s analyze the statement "Rock does not have wings" using the given information:.\n\n- From the context, we know that Rock is neither a fly nor a bird.\nRock definitely has wings, based on the information provided. All animals breathe, and Rock neither flies nor breathes, so it must have wings. Additionally, since Rock is not a mammal, it cannot be a monkey, bird, or fly. Therefore, Rock has wings.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
