messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIf people work in student jobs on campus, then they need to earn money to help pay for their college tuition. If people order takeout frequently in college, then they work in student jobs on campus. People either order takeout frequently in college or enjoy the dining hall meals and recipes. If people enjoy the dining hall meals and recipes, then they are not picky eaters. If people enjoy the dining hall meals and recipes, then they spend a lot of their time eating and catching up with friends in the campus dining halls. If Mary works in student jobs on campus and needs to earn money to help pay for her college tuition, then Mary is neither picky nor needs to earn money to help pay for her college tuition.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Mary is not a picky eater and spends a lot of her time eating and catching up with friends in the campus dining halls.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>.\nTo determine the truth of the statement "Mary is not a picky eater and spends a lot of her time eating and catching up with friends in the campus dining halls," we need to analyze the given context step by step and see if we can derive the necessary conditions for this statement to be true.\n\n1.**Mary works in student jobs on campus and needs to earn money to help pay for her college tuition.**.\n   - This is given directly in the context.\n\n2.**If people work in student jobs on campus, then they need to earn money to help pay for their college tuition.**.\n   - This is a restatement of the first point, confirming the necessity of earning money.\n\n3.**If people order takeout frequently in college, then they work in student jobs on campus.**.\n   - This implies that Mary, who works in student jobs, must order takeout frequently.\n\n4.**People either order takeout frequently in college or enjoy the dining hall meals and recipes.**.\n   - Since Mary orders takeout frequently, she does not enjoy the dining hall meals and recipes.\n\n5.**If people enjoy the dining hall meals and recipes, then they are not picky eaters.**.\n   - Since Mary does not enjoy the dining hall meals and recipes, she is not necessarily not picky eaters.However, we need to check if she is not picky eaters based on the given information.\n\n6.**If people enjoy the dining hall meals and recipes, then they spend a lot of their time eating and catching up with friends in the campus dining halls.**.\nSince Mary enjoys the dining hall meals and recipes, she frequently spends a lot of her time eating and catching up with friends in the campus dining halls.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
