\\(F\\)).\n\nWe want to determine if the following statement is true:\n- If a borrower does not incur additional financial penalties (\\(\\neg F\\)), then the borrower has a good credit score (\\(\\neg C\\)).\n\n**Step-by-Step Analysis:**\n\n1.**Original Statement:**\n   - \\( C \\rightarrow L \\)\n   - \\( L \\rightarrow P \\)\n   - \\( P \\rightarrow D \\)\n   - \\( D \\rightarrow \\neg F \\)\n\n2.**Contrapositive:**\n   - The contrapositive of \\( C \\rightarrow L \\) is \\( \\neg L \\rightarrow \\neg C \\).\n   - The contrapositive of \\( L \\rightarrow P \\) is \\( \\neg P \\rightarrow \\neg L \\).\n   - The contrapositive of \\( P \\rightarrow D \\) is \\( \\neg D \\rightarrow \\neg P \\).\n   - The contrapositive of \\( D \\rightarrow \\neg F \\) is \\( \\neg \\neg F \\rightarrow \\neg D \\) or \\( F \\rightarrow \\neg D \\).\n\n3.**Combining Contrapositives:**\n   - From \\( \\neg L \\rightarrow \\neg C \\) and \\( F \\rightarrow \\neg D \\), we can combine these to get:\n     - \\( \\neg F \\rightarrow \\neg C \\) (by transitivity of implication).\n\n4.**Conclusion:**\n   - The contrapositive \\( \\neg F \\rightarrow \\neg C \\) means that if a borrower does not incur additional financial penalties (\\(\\neg F\\)), then the borrower does not have a good credit score (\\(\\neg C\\)).\n\nTherefore, the original statement is false.\n\n**Financial Example:**\n- **Original Statement:**\n  - If a borrower has a good credit score (\\(C\\)), then they will be approved for a loan (\\(L\\)).\n  - If a borrower is approved for a loan (\\(L\\)), then they will make timely payments (\\(P\\)).\n  - If a borrower makes timely payments (\\(P\\)), then they will not default on the loan (\\(D\\)).\n  - If a borrower does not default on the loan (\\(D\\)), then they will not incur additional financial penalties (\\(F\\)).\n\n- **To Prove:**\n  - If a borrower does not incur additional financial penalties (\\(\\neg F\\)), then the borrower has a good credit score (\\(\\neg C\\