messages:   97%|#########7| 198/204 [03:27<00:05,  1.06it/s][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nAll mammals are animals. All monkeys are mammals. An animal is either a monkey or a bird. All birds fly. All animals breathe. If something can fly, then it has wings. If Rock is neither a fly nor a bird, then Rock neither flies nor breathes.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Rock has wings.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>.\nTo determine if the statement "Rock has wings" is true, false, or uncertain based on the given context, let\'s break down the information step by step:.\n\n1.**All mammals are animals.**.\n   - This establishes a direct relationship between mammals and animals.\n\n2.**All monkeys are mammals.**.\n   - This means that monkeys are a subset of mammals.\n\n3.**An animal is either a monkey or a bird.**.\n   - This categorizes animals into two groups: monkeys and birds.\n\n4.**All birds fly.**.\n   - This establishes that birds have the ability to fly.\n\n5.**All animals breathe.**.\n   - This establishes that animals have the ability to breathe.\n\n6.**If something can fly, then it has wings.**.\n   - This is a conditional statement that links the ability to fly with having wings.\n\n7.**If Rock is neither a fly nor a bird, then Rock neither flies nor breathes.**.\n   - This conditional statement provides a condition for Rock based on its classification.\n\nNow, let\'s analyze the information to determine if Rock has wings:.\n\n- **Rock is neither a fly nor a bird.**.\n  - According to the conditional statement, if Rock is neither a fly nor a bird, then Rock neither flies nor breathes.\n\n- **Rock neither flies nor breathes.**.\n  - Since Rock neither flies nor breathes, it cannot be a bird (as birds fly and breathe).\n\n- **Rock is not a bird.**.\n  - Therefore, Rock must be an animal (since Rock is neither a fly nor a bird).\n\n- **Rock is an animal.**.Rock has wings.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
